The "Additional Generators" section is described as containing "generators beyond the `Generators` factory," but it includes examples like `new FloatObjectGenerator(...)`, `new URLGenerator()`, and `new NonBlankStringGenerator()`. Factory methods for these exist in the `Generators` class (e.g., `Generators.floats(...)`, `Generators.urls()`), which could be confusing.

To improve clarity, I suggest focusing this section on generators that are genuinely outside the main factory, such as domain-specific generators or those with unique static helpers.

```
==== Additional Generators

The framework includes generators beyond the `Generators` factory, such as specialized date/time generators with static helper methods and various domain-specific generators.

[source,java]
----
// Date/Time with zones using static helper methods
var dateTime = ZonedDateTimeGenerator.any();

// Domain-specific generators (also available via GeneratorType enum)
var email = new EmailGenerator().next();
var city = new CityGenerator().next();
var name = new FullNameGenerator().next();
----
